The '''Torre Senador''' ({{lang|ca|Torre Senador}}; "Senator Tower") is a 52-storey mixed-use office and hotel tower at 600 [[Avinguda Embarcadero]] in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Completed in 1989, the tower houses the luxury [[Hotel Senador]] on its middle floors and office tenants on the lower and upper floors. It is one of the tallest buildings in the Sant Cristòfor waterfront skyline.

== Architecture ==

The Torre Senador consists of a blue-green glass shaft with a rectangular crown section. The tower has a regular floor plate from its base to near the top, where the crown is set back slightly and features a central notch or opening that gives the building a distinctive silhouette against the sky. The lower floors contain the hotel entrance, lobby, retail, restaurants, and conference facilities, while the middle floors are occupied by the Hotel Senador. The upper floors and the lower podium above the retail levels are occupied by office tenants.

The tower's footprint is approximately 2,000 to 2,500 m², with typical gross floor plates of approximately 1,900 to 2,300 m². The building's mixed-use configuration separates hotel and office circulation through dedicated elevator banks and service cores.

